@* What a page says back after a form acts, both halves at once: the one general message (Alert)
   and the list of field-bound errors (FormErrorSummary). See FormFeedback for which failure goes
   where. Every page with a form renders the pair, and a page that rendered one without the other
   would have a save that fails without saying how — so they are one component here, and the pair
   cannot be split by forgetting half of it.

   The dialogs render Alert alone on purpose: their fields are few and each carries its own
   FieldError, so a summary there would say everything twice. *@

<Alert Feedback="Feedback"/>
<FormErrorSummary Feedback="Feedback"/>

@code {
    /// <summary>The form's voice — usually the page's <c>_form</c>.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public FormFeedback Feedback { get; set; } = default!;
}
